# The same for a Set: `has` takes a SHARED lock for its duration, which the
# readonly iterator's shared pin coexists with. Two shared locks are exactly
# what the settled model allows.
main: function is {
    s: (Set String)
    s.add item: "a".string
    s.add item: "b".string
    with it: s.iterate do for x: it loop {
        h: s.has item: x
        print "x=\{x} h=\{h}"
    }
}
